**What session 165 accomplished — step-5 shadow-evaluator plumbing landed, tree builds clean:**

1. **Consumer-only victim-manifest read primitive** (`mxfs_dlm_caw_victim_manifest_read` in `dlm/dlm_caw.c`): given a resource and the fenced victim's heartbeat slot, returns whether the victim holds an exclusive-class grant there and under which `ex_grant_epoch`. Placed directly after the sess110 do-not-reintroduce comment with an explicit contra-sess110 contract — it answers "does the VICTIM hold EX here," never "what epoch may I stamp," so the deleted producer-misuse shape cannot come back through it.

2. **v5 wrappers** (`dlm/v5_mount.c/.h`): `mxfs_v5_dlm_victim_ag_manifest_read`, `mxfs_v5_dlm_victim_inode_manifest_read`, and `mxfs_v5_dlm_victim_recovery_read` (the capability check — reads the live recovery descriptor's stage/victim-identity off the victim's HB sector).

3. **xlog victim-slot threading** (`xfs/xfs_log_priv.h`, `xfs/xfs_log.c`): `struct xlog` gained `l_mxfs_victim_slot` (sentinel-initialized in `xlog_alloc_log`) and an eval-state pointer. The foreign-replay path binds the dead node's slot; the adopted-slice path binds our own slot with a comment explaining the expected all-not-held verdict there. Teardown hooks placed at all three exits (foreign-replay completion, `xfs_log_mount_finish`, `xlog_dealloc_log` backstop) via an idempotent `mxfs_shadow_eval_finish`.

4. **Verified with `make modules`** — mxfs.ko links cleanly with the plumbing in; zero behavior change so far (nothing allocates the eval state yet).

**Next session:** write the evaluator core in `xfs_log_recover.c` — the full per-token verdict spec (v1-never-evidence, class arms, owner/incarnation binding, manifest lookup with cache, per-transaction rollup, P273-SHADOW-CAP/-EVAL probes) is captured line-by-line in memory `ccloop-c7ee71c6-sess165-shadow-eval-plumbing-LANDED-evaluator-core-NEXT`, then bump to 0.11.460, RULE-5 consult on the diff, and rig-measure with a forced node kill. Also owed: ledger #7 next-field refresh and the 196-note compaction backlog.

